\"; \"]}]\n38:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-18\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-sāgarāt\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=sāgarāt\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"sāgarāt\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"from the ocean\"}}],\"; \"]}]\n39:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-19\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-bhavāmi\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=bhavāmi\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"bhavāmi\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"I become\"}}],\"; \"]}]\n3a:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-20\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-na\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=na\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"na\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"not\"}}],\"; \"]}]\n3b:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-21\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-cirāt\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=cirāt\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"cirāt\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"after a long time\"}}],\"; \"]}]\n3c:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-22\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-pārtha\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=pārtha\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"pārtha\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"O son of Pṛthā\"}}],\"; \"]}]\n3d:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-23\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-mayi\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=mayi\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"mayi\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"upon Me\"}}],\"; \"]}]\n3e:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-24\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-āveśita\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=āveśita\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"āveśita\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"fixed\"}}],\"; \"]}]\n3f:[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-25\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-cetasām\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=cetasām\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"cetasām\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"of those whose minds\"}}],\".\"]}]\n41:[\"$\",\"$L2a\",\"child-3524\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:6\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 e"])self.__next_f.push([1,"m-text-base text-center italic\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"yā vai sādhana-sampattiḥ
puruṣārtha-catuṣṭaye
tayā vinā tad āpnoti
naro nārāyaṇāśrayaḥ\"}}]}]\n42:[\"$\",\"$L2a\",\"child-3525\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:7\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"The purport of this verse is that one should not engage in the different processes of fruitive activity or cultivate knowledge by the mental speculative process. One who is devoted to the Supreme Personality can attain all the benefits derived from other yogic processes, speculation, rituals, sacrifices, charities, etc. That is the specific benediction of devotional service.\"}}]}]\n43:[\"$\",\"$L2a\",\"child-3526\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:8\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Simply by chanting the holy name of Kṛṣṇa – Hare Kṛṣṇa, Hare Kṛṣṇa, Kṛṣṇa Kṛṣṇa, Hare Hare/ Hare Rāma, Hare Rāma, Rāma Rāma, Hare Hare – a devotee of the Lord can approach the supreme destination easily and happily, but this destination cannot be approached by any other process of religion.\"}}]}]\n44:[\"$\",\"$L2a\",\"child-3527\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:9\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"The conclusion of Bhagavad-gītā is stated in the Eighteenth Chapter:\"}}]}]\n45:[\"$\",\"$L2a\",\"child-3528\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:10\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base text-center italic\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"sarva-dharmān parityajya
mām ekaṁ śaraṇaṁ vraja
ahaṁ tvāṁ sarva-pāpebhyo
mokṣayiṣyāmi mā śucaḥ\"}}]}]\n46:[\"$\",\"$L2a\",\"child-3529\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:11\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"One should give up all other processes of self-realization and simply execute devotional service in Kṛṣṇa consciousness. That will enable one to reach the highest perfection of life. There is no need for one to consider the sinful actions of his past life, because the Supreme Lord fully takes charge of him. Therefore one should not futilely try to deliver himself in spiritual realization. Let everyone take shelter of the supreme omnipotent Godhead, Kṛṣṇa. That is the highest perfection of life.\"}}]}]\n"])(function(){function c(){var b=a.contentDocument||(a.contentWindow&&a.contentWindow.document);if(b){var d=b.createElement(''script'');d.innerHTML="window.__CF$cv$params={r:''a34059aadfb4f501'',t:''MTc4ODIyNDU1NA==''};var a=document.createElement(''script'');a.src=''/cdn-cgi/challenge-platform/scripts/jsd/main.js'';document.getElementsByTagName(''head'')[0].appendChild(a);";b.getElementsByTagName(''head'')[0].appendChild(d)}}if(document.body){var a=document.createElement(''iframe'');a.height=1;a.width=1;a.style.position=''absolute'';a.style.top=0;a.style.left=0;a.style.border=''none'';a.style.visibility=''hidden'';document.body.appendChild(a);if(''loading''!==document.readyState)c();else if(window.addEventListener)document.addEventListener(''DOMContentLoaded'',c);else{var e=document.onreadystatechange||function(){};document.onreadystatechange=function(b){e(b);''loading''!==document.readyState&&(document.onreadystatechange=e,c())}}}})();', 'https://vedabase.io/en/library/bg/12/6-7/', true),
(12, '8', 8, 'class="av-devanagari">मय्येव मन आधत्स्व मयि बुद्धिं निवेशय ।
निवसिष्यसि मय्येव अत ऊर्ध्वं न संशय: ॥ ८ ॥

<div', 'class="av-verse_text">mayy eva mana ādhatsva
mayi buddhiṁ niveśaya
nivasiṣyasi mayy eva
ata ūrdhvaṁ na saṁśayaḥ

<div', 'class="av-synonyms">mayi — upon Me; eva — certainly; manaḥ — mind; ādhatsva — fix; mayi — upon Me; buddhim — intelligence; niveśaya — apply; nivasiṣyasi — you will live; mayi — in Me; eva — certainly; ataḥ ūrdhvam — thereafter; na — never; saṁśayaḥ — doubt.

<div', 'class="av-translation">Just fix your mind upon Me, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and engage all your intelligence in Me. Thus you will live in Me always, without a doubt.

<div', 'class="av-purport">One who is engaged in Lord Kṛṣṇa’s devotional service lives in a direct relationship with the Supreme Lord, so there is no doubt that his position is transcendental from the very beginning. A devotee does not live on the material plane – he lives in Kṛṣṇa. The holy name of the Lord and the Lord are nondifferent; therefore when a devotee chants Hare Kṛṣṇa, Kṛṣṇa and His internal potency are dancing on the tongue of the devotee. When he offers Kṛṣṇa food, Kṛṣṇa directly accepts these eatables, and the devotee becomes Kṛṣṇa-ized by eating the remnants. One who does not engage in such service cannot understand how this is so, although this is a process recommended in the Bhagavad-gītā and in other Vedic literatures.

TEXTS 6-7TEXT 9

